          {
            "title": "Question: For loops",
            "id": 79223,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we specify the number of times we want a for-loop to iterate?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">By adding a number inside <code>range()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">By creating a counter variable</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">We can't specify the number of repetitions we want a for loop to complete</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">By adding a number inside <code>range()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A number inside <code>range()</code> specifies how many times a for loop iterates.</p><p>Which line starts a loop that runs exactly four times?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>for i in range(4):</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>for i in range(3):</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>for i in range(5):</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>for i in range(4):</code>.</p></body></html>",
